# Wise Repository Instructions

Wise application source code is maintained in three or four separate
repositories under the user's source-repositories folder. Multiple
repositories may contribute to the same customer-facing product.

Search source repositories only when they are available in the active
workspace or through the provided tools. Do not assume that an unavailable
repository has been checked. Treat source repositories as read-only when
updating customer help documentation; make documentation changes only in
this repository unless explicitly asked otherwise.

Customer help documentation is stored in /docs as Markdown.

When working with documentation:

- Preserve existing terminology.
- Do not invent application functionality.
- Treat source code as evidence of current behavior.
- Treat existing documentation as the authority for customer-facing terminology.
- When source code and documentation disagree, flag the discrepancy.